%S A171701 3,8,18,24,48,60,120,120,180,336,360,360,720,720,720,840,1260,1440,
%T A171701 1680,1680,2520,2520,2520,2520,5040,5040,5040,5040,5040,5040,7560,
%U A171701 7560,10080,10080,10080,10080,15120,15120,15120,15120,20160,20160,25200,25200
%N A171701 The first n-fold (at least) intrinsically 2-palindromic number (in base ten).
%H A171701 Jeff Sponaugle, <a href="/A171701/b171701.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..1152</a> (Terms < 10^10)
%F A171701 If d'(k) is the number of divisors of k minus 1 for square k and minus 2 for numbers of the form m^2+m, then a(n) is the first k for which d'(k)/2>n-1.
%e A171701 a(1) = 3 is a palindrome, 11, in base 2.
%e A171701 a(2) = 8 is 2-fold 2-palindromic, 22 in base 3 and 11 in base 7.
%e A171701 a(3) = 18 is 3-fold 2-palindromic: 33 in base 5, 22 in base 8 and 11 in base 17.
%o A171701 (PARI) apply( {A171701(n)=for(k=n+2, oo, my(c=n); for(b=sqrtint(k)+1, k-1, Vecrev(d=digits(k, b))!=d || c-- || return(k)))}, [1..15]) \\ _M. F. Hasler_, Sep 29 2026
%Y A171701 Cf. A171702, A171703, A171704, A171705, A171706, A171740, A171741, A171742.
%K A171701 nonn,base,changed
